./ast
./ast-children
./ast-nodes
./row-range

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ StateSource is Tuple

` A case, continuation or fallback that names a case of a machine, with the case or
` continuation whose body it is written in, or none at the root.
+ node SyntaxId
+ owner SyntaxId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ extend AST

────────────────────
+ do state-items [SyntaxId]
    - body RowRange'SyntaxId

` The items of the body of a machine, a case or a continuation, with those of a machine
` written among them in its place, as the reference joins them.
. items [SyntaxId]
for item in children[body]
    do match? nodes[item]
        | .node-state-machine(row)
            for inner in state-items(row.body)
                items += inner
            continue
    items += item
= items

────────────────────
+ state-body RowRange'SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` The body of a machine, a case or a continuation; none of anything else.
match nodes[node]
    | .node-state-machine(row)
        row.body
    | .node-state-case(row)
        row.body
    | .node-state-continuation(row)
        row.body
    ??
        RowRange'SyntaxId()

────────────────────
+ state-name Atom?
    - node SyntaxId

` The case a case or a continuation enters, or a fallback clears.
match? nodes[node]
    | .node-state-case(row)
        row.name
    | .node-state-continuation(row)
        row.name
    | .node-state-fallback(row)
        row.target

────────────────────
+ state-trigger SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` The trigger of a case or a continuation, or none.
match nodes[node]
    | .node-state-case(row)
        row.trigger
    | .node-state-continuation(row)
        row.trigger
    ??
        0u32

────────────────────
+ state-targets RowRange'SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` What a case or a continuation gives the case it enters, or the values a fallback names.
match nodes[node]
    | .node-state-case(row)
        row.target
    | .node-state-continuation(row)
        row.target
    | .node-state-fallback(row)
        row.values
    ??
        RowRange'SyntaxId()

────────────────────
+ is-transition Bool
    - node SyntaxId

nodes[node] is .node-state-case || nodes[node] is .node-state-continuation

────────────────────
+ declared-machine SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId

` The state machine a declaration's value is, as the reference reads it, or none for any other
` value.
|? value == 0
    0
|? nodes[value] is .node-state-machine
    value
??
    0

────────────────────
+ do content-machines [SyntaxId]
    - content SyntaxId

` The state machines written as lines of a class's markup, each a line of its own, which the
` reference keeps on the object, each case's flag a property named after the case, in the order
` they run. Where a root `<This` holds the markup, those written beside it, before it and then
` after it; the reference declares no type for one among the root's lines.
. found [SyntaxId]
if content == 0
    = found
if root-this(content) != 0
    for machine in root-machines(content, false)
        found += machine
    for machine in root-machines(content, true)
        found += machine
    = found
do match? nodes[content-lines(content)]
    | .node-block(block)
        for statement in children[block.body]
            if nodes[statement] is .node-state-machine && runs-line(content, statement)
                found += statement
= found

────────────────────
+ do root-machines [SyntaxId]
    - content SyntaxId
    - after Bool

` The state machines written in a class's section beside its root `<This`: those before the
` root, or those `after` it. The reference runs them where they are written among the root's
` lines.
. found [SyntaxId]
. root = root-this(content)
if root == 0
    = found
. past = false
do match? nodes[content]
    | .node-content-block(row)
        do match? nodes[row.body]
            | .node-block(block)
                for statement in children[block.body]
                    if statement == root
                        past = true
                    else if past == after && nodes[statement] is .node-state-machine
                        found += statement
= found

────────────────────
+ declared-value SyntaxId
    - value SyntaxId

` What a declaration's value is evaluated as: the state machine it is, or the value.
if machine != 0 then machine else value

.. machine = declared-machine(value)

────────────────────
+ declared-local SyntaxId
    - pattern SyntaxId

` The name a declaration whose value is a state machine declares, or none: one name, with no
` type written.
match nodes[pattern]
    | .node-identifier
        pattern
    | .node-type-capture(row)
        if row.type == 0 && nodes[row.id] is .node-identifier then row.id else 0
    ??
        0

────────────────────
+ is-entry-item Bool
    - item SyntaxId

` Whether an item of a case's body runs as the case is entered: any but its cases,
` continuations, fallbacks, handlers and `do finally` blocks.
match nodes[item]
    | .node-for-block
        !is-state-handler(item)
    | .node-state-case
        false
    | .node-state-continuation
        false
    | .node-state-fallback
        false
    | .node-do-finally-block
        false
    ??
        true

────────────────────
+ do spawns-in-case Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - case SyntaxId

` Whether the activation of a case, among the cases of the machine whose body is `items`, owns a
` task spawned for it: one spawned in the body of the case, or of a continuation that enters it
` (`spawns-in-body`).
. name = state-name(case)
=? false if !name
if nodes[case] is .node-state-case && spawns-in-body(case)
    = true
for continuation in continuations-named(items, name)
    =? true if spawns-in-body(continuation)
= false

────────────────────
+ do spawns-in-body Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a task not marked `@detached` is spawned in an entry statement or a handler of the body
` of a case or a continuation. One spawned in a `do finally` block, or in a case or machine
` written in the body, is not.
for item in state-items(state-body(node))
    if (is-entry-item(item) || is-state-handler(item)) && nested-machine(item) == 0
        =? true if spawns-owned(item)
= false

────────────────────
+ do spawns-owned Bool
    - item SyntaxId

` Whether a task not marked `@detached` is spawned in a node, or in a node inside it.
for node in subtree-start(item) .. item
    do match? nodes[node]
        | .node-do-task-block(row)
            =? true if !row.detached
= false

────────────────────
+ do is-state-handler Bool
    - item SyntaxId

` Whether an item of a machine's body is a handler: a `for ... on` loop, which the case it is
` written in runs for each item of the loop's stream while the case is active.
do match? nodes[item]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        do match? nodes[row.loop]
            | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                = loop.is-subscriber
= false

────────────────────
+ do handler-loop SyntaxId
    - item SyntaxId

` The loop a handler runs by.
do match? nodes[item]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        = row.loop
= 0

────────────────────
+ group-trigger SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId

` Where a group of a body's event transitions keeps how its stream is read: its first
` transition's trigger, or a handler's loop.
if is-state-handler(head) then handler-loop(head) else state-trigger(head)

────────────────────
+ do group-stream SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId

` The stream a group of a body's event transitions, or a handler, is on.
if !is-state-handler(head)
    = trigger-stream(state-trigger(head))
do match? nodes[handler-loop(head)]
    | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
        = loop.container
= 0

────────────────────
+ do trigger-kind StateTriggerKind?
    - trigger SyntaxId

do match? nodes[trigger]
    | .node-state-trigger(row)
        = row.kind
= null

────────────────────
+ is-immediate Bool
    - trigger SyntaxId

` Whether a trigger is tested where its owner is entered, `if` or `if | p = s`, rather than
` on an event.
|? !kind
    false
??
    kind == .state-trigger-if || kind == .state-trigger-if-match

.. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)

────────────────────
+ is-immediate-transition Bool
    - item SyntaxId

` Whether a case or a continuation is tested where its owner is entered: one with an `if`
` trigger, or a continuation with no trigger, which always passes.
|? !is-transition(item)
    false
|? trigger == 0
    nodes[item] is .node-state-continuation
??
    is-immediate(trigger)

.. trigger = state-trigger(item)

────────────────────
+ do always-passes Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]

` Whether one of a body's immediate transitions is a continuation with no trigger, which always
` passes, so that where its owner settles, the reference never enters its first case.
for transition in immediate-transitions(items)
    if state-trigger(transition) == 0
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do trigger-item SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - position U32

do match? nodes[trigger]
    | .node-state-trigger(row)
        if position < row.items.count
            = children[row.items.start + position]
= 0

────────────────────
+ trigger-stream SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId

` The stream an event trigger is on.
|? !kind
    0
|? kind == .state-trigger-for-on || kind == .state-trigger-for-on-when
    trigger-item(trigger, 1)
|? kind == .state-trigger-on || kind == .state-trigger-on-when || kind == .state-trigger-when-stream
    trigger-item(trigger, 0)
|? kind == .state-trigger-whenever
    trigger-item(trigger, 0)
??
    0

.. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)

────────────────────
+ trigger-guard SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId

` The `when` a trigger tests after its pattern, or none.
|? !kind
    0
|? kind == .state-trigger-for-on-when
    trigger-item(trigger, 2)
|? kind == .state-trigger-on-when
    trigger-item(trigger, 1)
??
    0

.. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)

────────────────────
+ do trigger-pattern SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId

` The structure match a `for ... on` trigger takes each item with, or the one an `if | p = s`
` trigger tests its subject with.
. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)
if !kind
    = 0
if kind == .state-trigger-for-on || kind == .state-trigger-for-on-when
    = trigger-item(trigger, 0)
if kind == .state-trigger-if-match
    do match? nodes[trigger-item(trigger, 0)]
        | .node-state-match-expression(row)
            = row.pattern
= 0

────────────────────
+ do trigger-subject SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId

` What an `if | p = s` trigger tests.
. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)
if kind && kind == .state-trigger-if-match
    do match? nodes[trigger-item(trigger, 0)]
        | .node-state-match-expression(row)
            = row.subject
= 0

────────────────────
+ trigger-condition SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId

` What an `if` trigger tests.
|? kind && kind == .state-trigger-if
    trigger-item(trigger, 0)
??
    0

.. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)

────────────────────
+ do initial-case SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The case a body enters first: its first case with no trigger, or none.
for item in items
    do match? nodes[item]
        | .node-state-case(row)
            if row.trigger == 0
                = item
= 0

────────────────────
+ enters-initial Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - owner SyntaxId

` Whether the first case of a machine's body, or of a case or a continuation written in it, is
` entered and given what its own name is written with, as the reference enters it only where
` its owner settles: the machine's root, a continuation, a case a trigger enters or a
` continuation names, and the first case of an owner that settles. Where it gives nothing, the
` reference's entry is the same either way.
|? owner == 0
    true
|? initial == 0 || state-targets(initial).count == 0
    true
??
    settles(items, owner)

.. initial = initial-case(state-items(state-body(owner)))

────────────────────
_ settles Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - node SyntaxId

|? nodes[node] is .node-state-continuation || state-trigger(node) != 0
    true
|? continuations-named(items, state-name(node)!).length != 0
    true
|? path.length == 0
    true
|? initial-case(body) != node
    false
??
    path.length == 1 || settles(items, path[path.length - 2])

.. path = case-path(items, node)
.. body = if path.length == 1 then items else state-items(state-body(path[path.length - 2]))

────────────────────
+ do explicit-cases [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The cases written in a body and in the bodies of its cases, in the order written.
. found [SyntaxId]
for item in items
    if nodes[item] is .node-state-case
        found += item
        for inner in explicit-cases(state-items(state-body(item)))
            found += inner
= found

────────────────────
+ child-cases [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The cases written in a body itself.
each in items when nodes[each] is .node-state-case

────────────────────
+ do machine-cases [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` Every case a machine has, in the order of its union: each case written, and each case only
` a continuation enters or a fallback clears, where it first names it. A case written later
` takes the place of one only named before it.
. found [SyntaxId]
collect-cases(items, found)
= found

────────────────────
_ do collect-cases
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - found [SyntaxId]

for item in items
    . name = state-name(item)
    if !name
        continue
    . known = case-position(found, name)
    . explicit = nodes[item] is .node-state-case
    if known == null
        found += item
    else if explicit && !(nodes[found[known]] is .node-state-case)
        found[known] = item
    if !(nodes[item] is .node-state-fallback)
        collect-cases(state-items(state-body(item)), found)

────────────────────
+ do case-position U32?
    - cases [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` Where a case of a name is among a machine's cases.
for position in 0 .. < cases.length
    . named = state-name(cases[position])
    if named && named == name
        = position as U32
= null

────────────────────
+ do redefined-case SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The first case written again with the name of one written before it, or none.
. names [Atom]
= find-redefined(items, names)

────────────────────
_ do find-redefined SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - names [Atom]

for item in items
    do match? nodes[item]
        | .node-state-case(row)
            if names.find(row.name) != null
                = item
            names += row.name
    if is-transition(item)
        . inner = find-redefined(state-items(state-body(item)), names)
        if inner != 0
            = inner
= 0

────────────────────
+ do find-case SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` The case of a name written in a body or in the bodies of its cases, or none.
for item in items
    do match? nodes[item]
        | .node-state-case(row)
            if row.name == name
                = item
            . inner = find-case(state-items(row.body), name)
            if inner != 0
                = inner
= 0

────────────────────
+ do case-path [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - target SyntaxId

` The cases from the root of a body down to a case written in it, the case last, or none where
` it is not written there.
. found [SyntaxId]
for item in items
    if nodes[item] is .node-state-case
        if item == target
            found += item
            = found
        . inner = case-path(state-items(state-body(item)), target)
        if inner.length != 0
            found += item
            for below in inner
                found += below
            = found
= found

────────────────────
+ do path-to [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - node SyntaxId

` The cases from the root of a body down to a case, the case last; a continuation that enters a
` case none writes is alone.
. path = case-path(items, node)
if path.length == 0
    path += node
= path

────────────────────
+ do transition-depth Size
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - source SyntaxId
    - target SyntaxId

` Where a move from one case of a body to another leaves the paths from the root down to them,
` as the reference moves between them: past the cases the two share, but no further than the
` last case of either.
. leaving = path-to(items, source)
. entering = path-to(items, target)
. common = 0
while common < leaving.length && common < entering.length && leaving[common] == entering[common]
    common += 1
if common >= leaving.length
    common = leaving.length - 1
if common >= entering.length
    common = entering.length - 1
= common

────────────────────
+ do immediate-path [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - active SyntaxId
    - transition SyntaxId

` The cases an immediate transition of a case's body enters, as the reference passes it: a case
` alone; for a continuation, the cases of the path down to the case it names below the active
` case, or from where the two paths part, or the continuation alone where no case is written.
. path [SyntaxId]
if nodes[transition] is .node-state-case
    path += transition
    = path
. target = find-case(items, state-name(transition)!)
if target == 0
    path += transition
    = path
. down = path-to(items, target)
. place = down.find(active)
. below = place != null && place + 1 < down.length
. start = if below then place! + 1 else transition-depth(items, active, target)
for position in start .. < down.length
    path += down[position]
= path

────────────────────
+ do continuations-named [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` The continuations written in a body, and in the bodies of its cases and continuations, that
` enter the case of a name, in the order written.
. found [SyntaxId]
for item in items
    if !is-transition(item)
        continue
    if nodes[item] is .node-state-continuation && state-name(item)! == name
        found += item
    for inner in continuations-named(state-items(state-body(item)), name)
        found += inner
= found

────────────────────
+ immediate-transitions [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The cases and continuations of a body tested where its owner is entered, in order.
each in items when is-immediate-transition(each)

────────────────────
+ do immediate-fallback SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The fallback of a body's immediate transitions: the last written right after one of them.
. last-immediate = false
. found SyntaxId = 0
for item in items
    if is-immediate-transition(item)
        last-immediate = true
    else if is-transition(item) && state-trigger(item) != 0
        last-immediate = false
    else if nodes[item] is .node-state-fallback && last-immediate
        found = item
= found

────────────────────
+ do group-heads [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The first transition of each group of a body's event transitions, and each handler, in
` order. A group is the transitions whose triggers are on one stream; a handler is a group of
` its own.
. heads [SyntaxId]
for item in items
    if is-state-handler(item)
        heads += item
        continue
    if !is-transition(item)
        continue
    . trigger = state-trigger(item)
    if trigger == 0 || is-immediate(trigger)
        continue
    . known = false
    for head in heads
        if same-key(state-trigger(head), trigger)
            known = true
    if !known
        heads += item
= heads

────────────────────
+ do group-transitions [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - head SyntaxId

` The transitions of the group a transition heads, in order.
. found [SyntaxId]
. key = state-trigger(head)
for item in items
    if is-transition(item)
        . trigger = state-trigger(item)
        if trigger != 0 && !is-immediate(trigger) && same-key(key, trigger)
            found += item
= found

────────────────────
+ do group-fallback SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - head SyntaxId

` The fallback written after a transition of a group, with no immediate transition between.
. key = state-trigger(head)
. last SyntaxId = 0
. found SyntaxId = 0
for item in items
    if is-immediate-transition(item)
        last = 0
    else if is-transition(item) && state-trigger(item) != 0
        last = state-trigger(item)
    else if nodes[item] is .node-state-fallback && last != 0 && same-key(key, last)
        found = item
= found

────────────────────
+ do misplaced-fallback SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` A second fallback written in one body, which the reference rejects as it joins the body, or
` one written where no group of event transitions or immediate ones owns it, in a body or the
` bodies of its cases; or none.
. last-immediate = false
. last SyntaxId = 0
. seen = false
for item in items
    if is-immediate-transition(item)
        last-immediate = true
    else if is-transition(item) && state-trigger(item) != 0
        last-immediate = false
        last = state-trigger(item)
    else if nodes[item] is .node-state-fallback
        if seen || (!last-immediate && last == 0)
            = item
        seen = true
    if is-transition(item)
        . inner = misplaced-fallback(state-items(state-body(item)))
        if inner != 0
            = inner
= 0

────────────────────
+ same-key Bool
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` Whether two event triggers are on one stream, written alike, whatever their kinds.
|? is-immediate(left) || is-immediate(right) || !trigger-kind(left) || !trigger-kind(right)
    false
??
    same-stream(trigger-stream(left), trigger-stream(right))

────────────────────
+ alike-key Bool
    - other AST
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` Whether an event trigger is on a stream one of another tree is on, as `same-key` says.
|? is-immediate(left) || other.is-immediate(right) || !trigger-kind(left) || !other.trigger-kind(right)
    false
??
    alike-stream(other, trigger-stream(left), other.trigger-stream(right))

────────────────────
+ same-stream Bool
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` Whether two streams are written alike: names, members, calls, indexes, type arguments and
` literals of the same text. Anything else is alike only with itself.
left == right || alike-stream(this, left, right)

────────────────────
+ do alike-stream Bool
    - other AST
    - left SyntaxId
    - right SyntaxId

` Whether a stream is written as one of another tree is, as `same-stream` compares them, but
` for what is alike only with itself.
if left == 0 || right == 0
    = false
do match? nodes[left]
    | .node-identifier(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-identifier(theirs)
                = mine.name == theirs.name && mine.is-tracked == theirs.is-tracked
    | .node-get-expression(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-get-expression(theirs)
                if mine.name != theirs.name || mine.is-optional != theirs.is-optional
                    = false
                = alike-stream(other, mine.object, theirs.object)
    | .node-index-expression(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-index-expression(theirs)
                if mine.is-optional != theirs.is-optional
                    = false
                = alike-stream(other, mine.object, theirs.object) && same-index
                    .. same-index = alike-stream(other, mine.index, theirs.index)
    | .node-call-expression(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-call-expression(theirs)
                if mine.operands.count != theirs.operands.count || has-other-params
                    = false
                .. has-other-params = mine.param-count != theirs.param-count
                for offset in 0 .. < mine.operands.count
                    . given = children[mine.operands.start + offset]
                    if !alike-stream(other, given, other.children[theirs.operands.start + offset])
                        = false
                = alike-stream(other, mine.callable, theirs.callable)
    | .node-type-identifier(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-type-identifier(theirs)
                = mine.name == theirs.name && mine.is-declare == theirs.is-declare
    | .node-type-arguments(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-type-arguments(theirs)
                if mine.args.count != theirs.args.count
                    = false
                for offset in 0 .. < mine.args.count
                    . given = children[mine.args.start + offset]
                    if !alike-stream(other, given, other.children[theirs.args.start + offset])
                        = false
                = alike-stream(other, mine.base, theirs.base)
    | .node-integer-syntax(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-integer-syntax(theirs)
                = mine.value == theirs.value
    | .node-string-syntax(mine)
        do match? other.nodes[right]
            | .node-string-syntax(theirs)
                = mine.text == theirs.text
= false

────────────────────
+ do payload-source StateSource?
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` What gives a case's payload its type: of the cases, continuations and fallbacks that name it
` with targets, a `for ... on` one first, then one with any trigger, then a continuation or a
` fallback with none, then the case itself, the first of each. A continuation's body has the
` owner of the continuation.
. found [StateSource]
find-payload-sources(items, 0, name, found)
. best StateSource? = null
. score = 0u32
for source in found
    . given = source-score(source.node)
    if !best || given > score
        best = source
        score = given
= best

────────────────────
+ do payload-sources [StateSource]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` Each case, continuation and fallback that names a case with targets, in order, the source of
` its payload (`payload-source`) among them.
. found [StateSource]
find-payload-sources(items, 0, name, found)
= found

────────────────────
_ do find-payload-sources
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - owner SyntaxId
    - name Atom
    - found [StateSource]

for item in items
    . named = state-name(item)
    if !named
        continue
    if named == name && state-targets(item).count != 0
        found += StateSource(item, owner)
    do match? nodes[item]
        | .node-state-case
            find-payload-sources(state-items(state-body(item)), item, name, found)
        | .node-state-continuation
            find-payload-sources(state-items(state-body(item)), owner, name, found)

────────────────────
_ source-score U32
    - node SyntaxId

|? !kind
    if nodes[node] is .node-state-case then 0 else 1
|? kind == .state-trigger-for-on || kind == .state-trigger-for-on-when
    3
??
    2

.. trigger = state-trigger(node)
.. kind = trigger-kind(trigger)

────────────────────
_ do find-capture-sources
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - owner SyntaxId
    - cases [SyntaxId]
    - found [[StateSource]]

for item in items
    if !is-transition(item)
        continue
    if state-trigger(item) != 0
        . position = case-position(cases, state-name(item)!)
        if position != null
            found[position] += StateSource(item, owner)
    find-capture-sources(state-items(state-body(item)), item, cases, found)

────────────────────
+ do pattern-names
    - pattern SyntaxId
    - names [Atom]

` The names a trigger's pattern captures, as the reference types them: a captured name, the
` fields of a tuple, and the payload of a case.
do match? nodes[pattern]
    | .node-structure-match(row)
        pattern-names(row.pattern, names)
    | .node-type-capture(row)
        do match? nodes[row.id]
            | .node-identifier(named)
                if names.find(named.name) == null
                    names += named.name
    | .node-type-tuple(row)
        for field in children[row.field-types]
            pattern-names(field, names)
    | .node-type-case(row)
        pattern-names(row.value, names)

────────────────────
+ do target-names
    - node SyntaxId
    - names [Atom]

` The names among what a case or a continuation gives the case it enters.
for target in children[state-targets(node)]
    do match? nodes[target]
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if names.find(row.name) == null
                names += row.name

────────────────────
+ do machine-captures [[Atom]]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - cases [SyntaxId]

` The names each case of a machine keeps from what entered it, in the order of `cases`: of
` each case or continuation with a trigger that enters it, the names the activation it is
` written in sees where it inherits them (`inherits-owner`), and those its trigger's pattern
` captures, without the names it gives the case. The activation of a case sees the names of its
` targets and those it keeps, as far as they are known when its case is reached.
. kept [[Atom]]
. sources [[StateSource]]
for _ in cases
    . none [Atom]
    kept += none
    . unfound [StateSource]
    sources += unfound
find-capture-sources(items, 0, cases, sources)
for position in 0 .. < cases.length
    . names [Atom]
    for source in sources[position]
        . seen [Atom]
        if source.owner != 0 && inherits-owner(source.node)
            target-names(source.owner, seen)
            . owner-name = state-name(source.owner)!
            . owner-position = case-position(cases, owner-name)
            if owner-position != null
                for inner in kept[owner-position]
                    if seen.find(inner) == null
                        seen += inner
        pattern-names(trigger-pattern(state-trigger(source.node)), seen)
        . given [Atom]
        target-names(source.node, given)
        for inner in seen
            if given.find(inner) == null && names.find(inner) == null
                names += inner
    kept[position] = names
= kept

────────────────────
+ do inherits-owner Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether the activation of a case entered by a transition sees the names the activation the
` transition is written in sees, as the reference captures them: a case's does, and a
` continuation's where its body writes transitions of its own.
if nodes[node] is .node-state-case
    = true
for item in children[state-body(node)]
    if is-transition(item)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
+ do nested-machine SyntaxId
    - item SyntaxId

` The machine a property written in a case's body is, a named machine of its own, or none: its
` value, or the one statement of a block written for it, where it names no type.
do match? nodes[item]
    | .node-property-syntax(row)
        do match? nodes[row.left]
            | .node-type-capture(left)
                if left.type == 0
                    = declared-machine(row.value)
= 0

────────────────────
+ do nested-machine-name Atom?
    - item SyntaxId

` The name of the property a named machine written in a case's body is.
do match? nodes[item]
    | .node-property-syntax(row)
        do match? nodes[row.left]
            | .node-type-capture(left)
                do match? nodes[left.id]
                    | .node-identifier(named)
                        = named.name
= null

────────────────────
+ nested-machines [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The items of a body that are named machines written in it, in order.
each in items when nested-machine(each) != 0
